The votes were counted at the Windrush Leisure Centre in [[Witney]]. The turnout was given as 39 percent.<ref name="Oxon 2022 live">{{Cite news|author=Sofia Della Sala |url=https://www.oxfordshirelive.co.uk/news/oxfordshire-news/west-oxfordshire-local-elections-2022-7039906 |title=West Oxfordshire local elections 2022: Live updates from the overnight count |work=OxfordshireLive |date=6 May 2022 |access-date=5 August 2022 }}</ref> Following these election results the Conservatives lost control of West Oxfordshire after being in charge for 22 years. The deputy leader of the council lost his seat.<ref name="BBC Oxon results">{{Cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-oxfordshire-61344065 |title=Tories lose control of West Oxfordshire Council in local election results 2022 |date=6 May 2022 |access-date=5 August 2022 |work=[[BBC News]]}}</ref>

